1
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:04,943
PREVIOUSLY ON <i>TATSUKI: TOO KIND FOR SCHOOL</i>

2
00:00:05,009 --> 00:00:06,678
It's pointless if it's not perfect.

3
00:00:06,744 --> 00:00:08,146
Why did you make a mistake?

4
00:00:08,213 --> 00:00:10,081
You want to win the gold medal, right?

5
00:00:10,148 --> 00:00:11,883
<i>I think there's a possibility</i>

6
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:14,752
that Umine is being subjected
to "tiger parenting."

7
00:00:14,819 --> 00:00:15,720
<i>When I see Umine,</i>

8
00:00:15,787 --> 00:00:17,188
<i>I'm reminded of myself</i>

9
00:00:17,255 --> 00:00:19,224
<i>when I was a child.</i>
<i>So I feel the need to do something.</i>

10
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:21,359
I understand how you feel,
but you should step back.

11
00:00:21,426 --> 00:00:24,229
Then who is going to
look after her instead?

12
00:00:24,295 --> 00:00:25,897
Who'll listen to her cries for help?

13
00:00:25,964 --> 00:00:27,165
Calm down.

14
00:00:27,665 --> 00:00:29,868
Take some time off work.

15
00:00:30,635 --> 00:00:32,637
All I did was hurt you. I'm really sorry.

16
00:00:35,874 --> 00:00:37,041
<i>What's the matter?</i>

17
00:00:37,108 --> 00:00:39,177
She barricaded herself inside.

18
00:00:39,244 --> 00:00:40,311
What?

19
00:00:40,378 --> 00:00:42,447
Umine, come on out.

20
00:00:43,047 --> 00:00:44,282
Call Daddy.

21
00:00:44,949 --> 00:00:46,017
What?

22
00:00:53,625 --> 00:00:55,026
Call Tatsuki.

23
00:00:56,261 --> 00:00:58,062
Sorry, I have to go.

24
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:01,432
-You didn't used to be like this.
-What?

25
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,969
You never helped me when I needed it.

26
00:01:11,242 --> 00:01:12,977
You need to go, right?

27
00:01:21,786 --> 00:01:23,588
Sorry, I'll contact you later.

28
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,174
Tatsuki's here.

29
00:01:43,775 --> 00:01:45,210
-Where've you been?
-Hey there.

30
00:01:45,276 --> 00:01:46,578
-Welcome back.
-Mr. Tatsuki.

31
00:01:46,644 --> 00:01:47,745
Where's Umine?

32
00:01:47,812 --> 00:01:49,280
She locked herself in the room.

33
00:01:55,453 --> 00:01:56,321
Umine.

34
00:01:57,622 --> 00:01:58,456
Sorry.

35
00:02:04,128 --> 00:02:05,330
Can you let me come inside?

36
00:02:31,756 --> 00:02:32,657
What's the matter?

37
00:02:37,528 --> 00:02:39,230
You broke your promise.

38
00:02:41,399 --> 00:02:43,568
You said you'd be by my side
no matter what.

39
00:02:44,502 --> 00:02:46,971
Sorry, I had family matters to attend to.

40
00:02:48,206 --> 00:02:50,708
I was being good, you know.

41
00:02:55,246 --> 00:02:57,215
Want to do something? How about drawing?

42
00:02:57,282 --> 00:02:58,116
No.

43
00:03:01,052 --> 00:03:02,720
I have homework for cram school.

44
00:03:07,759 --> 00:03:08,826
We'll be going now.

45
00:03:08,893 --> 00:03:10,128
-Bye.
-Bye.

46
00:03:10,194 --> 00:03:12,430
-Bye. Stay safe.
-Bye.

47
00:03:12,497 --> 00:03:14,399
-Hello.
-Hello.

48
00:03:14,465 --> 00:03:15,400
Hello.

49
00:03:15,466 --> 00:03:17,135
-Hello.
-Hello.

50
00:03:17,201 --> 00:03:18,336
I'll go call Umine.

51
00:03:18,403 --> 00:03:19,304
Thank you.

52
00:03:21,839 --> 00:03:24,509
Umine, your dad is here.

53
00:03:30,481 --> 00:03:32,750
You can stay longer, if you want.

54
00:03:33,718 --> 00:03:34,552
Mr. Tatsuki.

55
00:03:37,755 --> 00:03:38,823
I'll go.

56
00:03:46,297 --> 00:03:48,766
Do you think Tatsuki is all right?

57
00:03:51,336 --> 00:03:52,570
I wonder.

58
00:04:04,315 --> 00:04:05,650
Um…

59
00:04:07,018 --> 00:04:09,687
I'll be leaving now.

60
00:04:09,754 --> 00:04:10,788
What will you be…?

61
00:04:11,356 --> 00:04:12,790
Oh.

62
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:15,793
I was told to take time off work,

63
00:04:16,994 --> 00:04:18,429
but I have nowhere else to go.

64
00:04:20,598 --> 00:04:22,033
Can I stay here?

65
00:04:24,469 --> 00:04:25,570
I'm sure that's okay.

66
00:04:27,538 --> 00:04:28,506
Sorry.

67
00:04:31,509 --> 00:04:33,878
Then, I'll be going now.

68
00:04:59,537 --> 00:05:01,472
YUKANAI

69
00:05:01,539 --> 00:05:04,442
COUNTERTRANSFERENCE

70
00:05:08,379 --> 00:05:10,815
TATSUKI IS RESTING

71
00:05:14,719 --> 00:05:15,620
Good morning.

72
00:05:16,187 --> 00:05:17,021
Good morning.

73
00:05:17,088 --> 00:05:21,325
We have to start getting ready
for the middle school graduation party.

74
00:05:21,893 --> 00:05:22,927
You're right.

75
00:05:23,494 --> 00:05:26,497
This year, Tomoki and Tonetaku
are graduating.

76
00:05:27,064 --> 00:05:28,533
I see.

77
00:05:34,739 --> 00:05:36,274
UMINE

78
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:38,342
I HAVE TO STUDY AGAIN…

79
00:05:41,245 --> 00:05:46,050
IF YOU CAN'T HANDLE IT…

80
00:05:47,819 --> 00:05:49,153
<i>If you lose your head over this,</i>

81
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:51,322
you won't be able to save her.

82
00:06:23,521 --> 00:06:25,356
Kae, you're good at this.

83
00:06:25,423 --> 00:06:26,524
-Really?
-Yeah.

84
00:06:27,391 --> 00:06:29,227
How can I make it into a triangle?

85
00:06:29,293 --> 00:06:32,430
Curve your hand like this,

86
00:06:32,497 --> 00:06:33,998
and rotate it like this.

87
00:06:34,065 --> 00:06:37,468
But it'll turn into a round ball.

88
00:06:37,535 --> 00:06:38,870
No way.

89
00:06:38,936 --> 00:06:40,538
Is Tatsuki not feeling well?

90
00:06:41,706 --> 00:06:43,875
Seems like it. We should let him rest.

91
00:06:44,442 --> 00:06:46,711
I guess I'll be nice
and deliver a rice ball.

92
00:06:46,777 --> 00:06:48,346
Good idea.

93
00:06:48,412 --> 00:06:51,115
I bet Tatsuki is hungry.

94
00:06:51,182 --> 00:06:52,717
But isn't the door locked?

95
00:06:52,783 --> 00:06:53,651
TATSUKI IS RESTING

96
00:06:53,718 --> 00:06:54,952
Then…

97
00:06:55,019 --> 00:06:56,621
Can Kae and Sakurako take it to him?

98
00:07:01,292 --> 00:07:05,096
Rice balls, rice balls.

99
00:07:07,431 --> 00:07:10,301
Would you like some
freshly made rice balls?

100
00:07:12,203 --> 00:07:13,304
Thank you.

101
00:07:14,405 --> 00:07:16,307
Tatsuki, are you not feeling well?

102
00:07:18,442 --> 00:07:20,444
Just a little. But no worries.

103
00:07:22,313 --> 00:07:25,516
This one is salted kelp,
but guess what flavor

104
00:07:25,583 --> 00:07:26,617
the other one is.

105
00:07:27,785 --> 00:07:28,819
What could it be?

106
00:07:29,554 --> 00:07:30,588
Is it bonito flakes?

107
00:07:30,655 --> 00:07:34,692
Eat it and you'll find out.

108
00:07:38,763 --> 00:07:40,331
Okay,

109
00:07:41,566 --> 00:07:43,034
then I'll try it.

110
00:07:49,373 --> 00:07:51,442
-How is it?
-Is it good?

111
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:54,011
It's strawberry!

112
00:07:58,049 --> 00:08:00,384
But it's actually not that bad.

113
00:08:01,452 --> 00:08:03,554
Thank you for your business.

114
00:08:03,621 --> 00:08:04,989
Please excuse us.

115
00:08:05,056 --> 00:08:06,490
Thank you.

116
00:08:24,275 --> 00:08:26,110
-Can I come in?
-Yeah.

117
00:08:29,246 --> 00:08:31,515
I told you to take time off work,

118
00:08:32,049 --> 00:08:33,951
but you don't have
anywhere else to go, huh?

119
00:08:34,018 --> 00:08:35,987
Yeah, sorry.

120
00:08:36,587 --> 00:08:39,824
It seems like Umine will also be taking
some time off for the math competition.

121
00:08:40,558 --> 00:08:41,859
I see.

122
00:08:45,162 --> 00:08:48,165
I wonder if Umine is doing all right.

123
00:08:50,101 --> 00:08:51,268
I wonder.

124
00:09:10,154 --> 00:09:14,358
Why are you so worried about Umine?

125
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:20,331
I don't know why.

126
00:09:21,632 --> 00:09:24,502
But whenever I see Umine,

127
00:09:25,336 --> 00:09:28,673
<i>memories of my own childhood</i>
<i>cross my mind.</i>

128
00:09:38,315 --> 00:09:39,450
What is it guys?

129
00:09:42,553 --> 00:09:43,621
All right.

130
00:09:44,121 --> 00:09:45,623
-You guys can come in now.
-Tatsuki.

131
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:48,059
-Tatsuki.
-How are you doing?

132
00:09:48,125 --> 00:09:50,294
-Tatsuki, are you all right?
-Yeah, I'm all right.

133
00:09:51,862 --> 00:09:53,831
Okay, let's all draw together!

134
00:09:54,398 --> 00:09:56,434
-Yeah!
-Hooray!

135
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,568
What are we drawing?

136
00:09:57,635 --> 00:09:58,569
Anything we want?

137
00:09:58,636 --> 00:09:59,904
Should we use the new paint?

138
00:09:59,970 --> 00:10:01,739
-Good idea.
-Then

139
00:10:01,806 --> 00:10:03,841
let's draw a nostalgic scene
from your childhood.

140
00:10:03,908 --> 00:10:05,142
I'm still a child.

141
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:06,610
You're right.

142
00:10:06,677 --> 00:10:08,979
Then from when you were really little.
Do you remember anything?

143
00:10:09,547 --> 00:10:10,881
I have to think about it.

144
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:13,651
Tatsuki, you should draw too.

145
00:10:13,718 --> 00:10:14,552
What?

146
00:10:14,618 --> 00:10:16,887
Scenery I saw when I was little?

147
00:10:18,422 --> 00:10:20,324
Scenery that remains
in your memory even now.

148
00:10:24,395 --> 00:10:25,329
Okay.

149
00:10:41,312 --> 00:10:43,647
I'm always impressed
by your drawing skills, Tatsuki.

150
00:10:45,182 --> 00:10:46,684
Were you always good at it?

151
00:10:48,018 --> 00:10:49,320
I'm not sure.

152
00:10:50,354 --> 00:10:52,156
But I always loved to draw.

153
00:11:09,073 --> 00:11:10,241
What's the matter?

154
00:11:11,008 --> 00:11:11,842
It's nothing.

155
00:11:15,579 --> 00:11:18,549
All right, how about we step outside

156
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,417
for a change of pace.

157
00:11:23,988 --> 00:11:25,523
Get in.

158
00:11:26,223 --> 00:11:27,057
Okay.

159
00:11:31,262 --> 00:11:32,730
Where are we going?

160
00:11:32,797 --> 00:11:34,064
I haven't decided.

161
00:11:36,167 --> 00:11:37,701
We'll go where the wind takes us.

162
00:11:40,437 --> 00:11:42,239
So you got to talk with Sora, huh?

163
00:11:42,306 --> 00:11:43,140
Yes.

164
00:11:43,908 --> 00:11:47,244
But I've done some pretty awful things…

165
00:11:48,412 --> 00:11:51,248
So when I had to rush back to Yukanai
for Umine,

166
00:11:51,882 --> 00:11:54,151
he told me,
"You didn't used to be like this."

167
00:11:56,086 --> 00:11:59,190
And he said, "You never helped me
when I needed it."

168
00:12:01,692 --> 00:12:03,828
I was at a loss for words.

169
00:12:06,263 --> 00:12:09,300
Well, it looks like it's going to take
a little more time

170
00:12:09,366 --> 00:12:11,235
before your feelings get across to him.

171
00:12:20,878 --> 00:12:24,515
So why did you stop drawing
halfway through?

172
00:12:27,151 --> 00:12:29,486
For a moment, I was reminded of a moment

173
00:12:29,987 --> 00:12:31,288
in my childhood.

174
00:12:32,990 --> 00:12:35,426
I have a memory of drawing a vivid,

175
00:12:35,993 --> 00:12:39,163
fiery-red sky for a school assignment
or something.

176
00:12:40,531 --> 00:12:43,400
Though, come to think of it,
it's probably not a fond memory.

177
00:12:46,170 --> 00:12:47,404
I see.

178
00:12:50,841 --> 00:12:52,610
What were you like as a kid?

179
00:12:55,646 --> 00:12:59,750
I was relatively quiet,
and studied pretty diligently.

180
00:13:00,918 --> 00:13:03,621
My father was big on education,
so he was quite strict.

181
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:07,992
How is your relationship
with your dad now?

182
00:13:09,526 --> 00:13:12,563
We don't really talk much,
but I'd say it's pretty normal.

183
00:13:13,831 --> 00:13:14,732
I see.

184
00:13:15,232 --> 00:13:16,166
Then I guess it's okay.

185
00:13:16,767 --> 00:13:17,768
What's okay?

186
00:13:18,636 --> 00:13:20,804
-Let's go to your parents' house.
-What?

187
00:13:21,205 --> 00:13:22,873
Now?

188
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,541
Put the address in the GPS.

189
00:13:25,109 --> 00:13:26,343
Are you serious?

190
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:28,445
COUNTERTRANSFERENCE

191
00:13:28,512 --> 00:13:29,980
You're studying something?

192
00:13:33,784 --> 00:13:36,754
Umine calls Mr. Tatsuki "Daddy,"

193
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:40,391
and directs the kind of feelings
one holds for a parent toward him.

194
00:13:41,325 --> 00:13:42,559
Yeah.

195
00:13:42,626 --> 00:13:46,263
According to Professor Mikuko,
that's called transference.

196
00:13:47,998 --> 00:13:51,168
And Mr. Tatsuki was also

197
00:13:51,235 --> 00:13:54,305
deeply invested emotionally
when it concerned Umine, right?

198
00:13:55,873 --> 00:13:57,808
Oh, that's called countertransference?

199
00:13:57,875 --> 00:13:58,876
Right.

200
00:13:58,943 --> 00:14:02,413
I mean, it doesn't necessarily mean
that it's a bad thing, though.

201
00:14:03,747 --> 00:14:05,149
That's what you're studying?

202
00:14:07,051 --> 00:14:09,687
I was wondering
if there was anything I could do

203
00:14:09,753 --> 00:14:13,490
while Mr. Tatsuki is taking a break.

204
00:14:17,561 --> 00:14:21,098
Oh, speaking of, tomorrow is Umine's
mathematics competition, isn't it?

205
00:14:22,733 --> 00:14:24,101
Yeah.

206
00:14:29,206 --> 00:14:32,076
NATIONAL MATHEMATICS COMPETITION
"THAT'S RIGHT" MOCK EXAM

207
00:14:43,787 --> 00:14:44,788
Come in.

208
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:49,893
-Hey.
-Tatsuki, what a surprise.

209
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:52,096
This is Mr. Mikumo from my workplace.

210
00:14:52,162 --> 00:14:53,097
-Hello.
-Hello.

211
00:14:53,163 --> 00:14:55,265
Please come inside.

212
00:14:55,332 --> 00:14:57,067
Oh my.

213
00:14:58,802 --> 00:14:59,937
Hey, dear.

214
00:15:03,107 --> 00:15:03,974
What's with that hair?

215
00:15:04,675 --> 00:15:05,776
That's my dad.

216
00:15:05,843 --> 00:15:07,611
Hello, nice to meet you.

217
00:15:08,645 --> 00:15:12,249
I'm Mikumo, the representative
at an alternative school called Yukanai.

218
00:15:12,316 --> 00:15:15,352
-Thank you for helping out my son.
-Not at all.

219
00:15:15,419 --> 00:15:18,389
I really was just passing by,
so I’ll be taking my leave now.

220
00:15:19,356 --> 00:15:20,224
Hold on.

221
00:15:20,290 --> 00:15:22,426
I'll come back to pick you up.
So rest well.

222
00:15:22,493 --> 00:15:25,329
-You've got to be kidding.
-Please stay and eat with us.

223
00:15:25,396 --> 00:15:27,464
-Thank you, but please don't mind me.
-Don't leave me.

224
00:15:27,531 --> 00:15:28,699
Come over here, dear.

225
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,268
Please stay for a while.

226
00:15:32,002 --> 00:15:33,904
You have to listen to my dad.

227
00:15:34,805 --> 00:15:35,873
Fine.

228
00:15:35,939 --> 00:15:38,509
Thank you for your kind offer.

229
00:15:38,575 --> 00:15:39,910
Would you like to take a bath?

230
00:15:39,977 --> 00:15:41,612
I'm fine, thank you.

231
00:16:30,994 --> 00:16:34,498
AWARD CERTIFICATE

232
00:16:37,234 --> 00:16:40,404
All right, so what do you think
the protagonist is feeling

233
00:16:40,471 --> 00:16:42,306
-in this scene?
-I know!

234
00:16:42,372 --> 00:16:43,340
Me!

235
00:16:43,407 --> 00:16:44,641
Okay, Koike.

236
00:16:44,708 --> 00:16:46,743
She's feeling sad.

237
00:16:46,810 --> 00:16:48,212
That's correct.

238
00:16:49,947 --> 00:16:50,781
Yes, Ukita?

239
00:16:52,282 --> 00:16:53,884
Is that really the correct answer?

240
00:16:53,951 --> 00:16:55,352
What?

241
00:16:55,919 --> 00:16:57,554
It might not just be sadness.

242
00:16:57,621 --> 00:16:59,289
There might also be feelings of relief.

243
00:16:59,356 --> 00:17:01,625
-But the husband died…
-Or she might be spaced out.

244
00:17:01,692 --> 00:17:04,261
But she lost someone very dear to her…

245
00:17:04,328 --> 00:17:06,497
Is there really only one answer?

246
00:17:06,563 --> 00:17:07,898
That's enough.

247
00:17:16,773 --> 00:17:18,075
For your art homework,

248
00:17:18,142 --> 00:17:21,678
please draw a picture
of your favorite type of sky, okay?

249
00:17:21,745 --> 00:17:23,514
Yes.

250
00:17:24,748 --> 00:17:26,116
-I'll draw a whale-shaped cloud.
-Nice.

251
00:17:43,433 --> 00:17:45,035
What are you drawing?

252
00:17:45,836 --> 00:17:48,572
It's my homework. I'm drawing the sky.

253
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:51,875
Why is it red?

254
00:17:57,147 --> 00:17:58,582
That doesn't look like a sky.

255
00:17:59,383 --> 00:18:00,484
Draw it properly.

256
00:18:01,585 --> 00:18:02,519
‎What?

257
00:18:04,054 --> 00:18:05,355
Stop messing around,

258
00:18:05,422 --> 00:18:08,659
and draw it properly
so that it actually looks like a sky.

259
00:18:13,163 --> 00:18:14,031
Got it?

260
00:18:16,833 --> 00:18:17,701
Yes.

261
00:18:19,937 --> 00:18:21,505
Ukita's artwork

262
00:18:21,572 --> 00:18:25,142
was selected for the city art contest!
Let's hear it for him!

263
00:18:25,209 --> 00:18:27,778
-Wow!
-You're amazing!

264
00:18:27,844 --> 00:18:29,146
Come up here, Ukita.

265
00:18:30,013 --> 00:18:32,082
-Yes.
-You're the best!

266
00:18:32,149 --> 00:18:34,117
Congratulations.

267
00:18:34,184 --> 00:18:35,686
Show it to everyone.

268
00:18:35,752 --> 00:18:37,487
Let's give him a round of applause.

269
00:18:37,554 --> 00:18:39,823
Wow!

270
00:18:45,128 --> 00:18:47,698
See? I was right, wasn't I?

271
00:18:48,265 --> 00:18:50,234
It really was the right call to redraw it.

272
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,970
You're amazing, Tatsuki.

273
00:19:42,419 --> 00:19:44,655
Which university are you applying for?

274
00:19:48,692 --> 00:19:51,695
After I graduate high school,
I want to study art.

275
00:19:55,499 --> 00:19:57,901
I want to go to a vocational school
specializing in arts.

276
00:19:58,468 --> 00:20:00,003
A vocational school?

277
00:20:05,275 --> 00:20:07,377
What you want to study

278
00:20:07,444 --> 00:20:10,380
is up to you to decide,
so just do whatever you like.

279
00:20:11,381 --> 00:20:14,151
But you have to go to university.

280
00:20:14,851 --> 00:20:16,019
What?

281
00:20:16,086 --> 00:20:18,388
You might not be able
to make a living from art.

282
00:20:19,690 --> 00:20:23,260
Wouldn't going to university
broaden your options?

283
00:20:26,163 --> 00:20:27,497
Is that really so?

284
00:20:28,565 --> 00:20:30,200
Go to university.

285
00:20:30,967 --> 00:20:32,803
Your grades aren't bad, after all.

286
00:20:45,415 --> 00:20:47,884
Hey, where's my sketchbook?

287
00:20:47,951 --> 00:20:50,554
It was creating a mess,
so I put it out with the recyclables.

288
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:52,356
What? Why?

289
00:20:52,422 --> 00:20:56,193
I told you to clean up so many times,
but you never got around to it.

290
00:20:56,259 --> 00:20:58,161
Why did you throw it away?

291
00:20:59,529 --> 00:21:02,432
Don't get so angry with me.

292
00:21:02,499 --> 00:21:03,900
You don't need it for the entrance exams.

293
00:21:12,976 --> 00:21:15,112
This was your room?

294
00:21:16,213 --> 00:21:19,282
Yeah, although it's being used
as a storage room now.

295
00:21:21,118 --> 00:21:22,652
You held on to your work, huh?

296
00:21:24,221 --> 00:21:25,188
Look at this.

297
00:21:26,289 --> 00:21:30,026
Dad told me that this doesn't look
like a drawing of the sky.

298
00:21:31,094 --> 00:21:32,462
So I redrew it, and here it is.

299
00:21:34,731 --> 00:21:35,899
I see.

300
00:21:35,966 --> 00:21:39,469
When I did what my dad told me to do,
I ended up winning an award.

301
00:21:40,203 --> 00:21:43,540
From then on, all focus turned
to winning awards.

302
00:21:44,908 --> 00:21:45,809
Even though

303
00:21:47,043 --> 00:21:50,180
I came to love drawing because
it allowed me to express myself freely.

304
00:21:51,815 --> 00:21:53,183
I see.

305
00:21:56,253 --> 00:21:59,055
I think the reason why I can't stop
being concerned about Umine

306
00:22:00,824 --> 00:22:03,326
is because her situation
is similar to my own childhood.

307
00:22:05,061 --> 00:22:06,129
I worry

308
00:22:06,897 --> 00:22:10,100
that she's suffering from the pressure
to produce good results.

309
00:22:11,735 --> 00:22:14,271
You might be right.

310
00:22:20,243 --> 00:22:22,245
I wonder what kind of feelings

311
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:25,982
you dad had toward you back then.

312
00:22:26,550 --> 00:22:29,519
My dad's feelings?

313
00:22:34,958 --> 00:22:36,760
Is Sora doing well?

314
00:22:44,968 --> 00:22:46,069
You still see him?

315
00:22:46,837 --> 00:22:47,804
I saw him recently.

316
00:22:47,871 --> 00:22:49,039
I see.

317
00:22:50,307 --> 00:22:52,909
We were worried about
how things have been since the divorce.

318
00:23:09,693 --> 00:23:11,595
You fish?

319
00:23:12,229 --> 00:23:13,964
Yeah, you didn't know?

320
00:23:15,098 --> 00:23:16,399
I never saw him fishing.

321
00:23:17,934 --> 00:23:19,903
Well, he was always buried in work.

322
00:23:19,970 --> 00:23:21,304
But now he has the time.

323
00:23:21,805 --> 00:23:22,939
Wanna go together?

324
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:27,010
No, thanks.

325
00:23:28,078 --> 00:23:29,312
It's fun.

326
00:23:32,148 --> 00:23:33,850
Go take a bath.

327
00:23:36,553 --> 00:23:37,387
Okay.

328
00:23:41,825 --> 00:23:44,427
I didn't know that fishing was your hobby.

329
00:23:47,130 --> 00:23:48,431
I started after I retired.

330
00:23:50,867 --> 00:23:53,537
I thought you weren't the type
who could sit still like this.

331
00:23:55,805 --> 00:23:57,641
Yeah, now that you mention it.

332
00:23:58,642 --> 00:23:59,776
I guess you changed.

333
00:24:01,645 --> 00:24:02,679
Probably.

334
00:24:08,652 --> 00:24:10,120
When I was a kid

335
00:24:12,289 --> 00:24:15,759
I won an award
for drawing a picture of a blue sky.

336
00:24:16,927 --> 00:24:17,861
Do you remember?

337
00:24:20,096 --> 00:24:21,798
A drawing of a blue sky?

338
00:24:22,799 --> 00:24:25,702
I don't remember.

339
00:24:29,306 --> 00:24:30,307
I figured.

340
00:24:32,075 --> 00:24:34,778
But I remember you were good at drawing.

341
00:24:39,049 --> 00:24:41,418
Why do you bring that up?

342
00:24:49,225 --> 00:24:53,096
At first, I had drawn a red sky,

343
00:24:54,097 --> 00:24:55,665
but I was forced to redraw it.

344
00:24:56,533 --> 00:24:57,400
By whom?

345
00:24:58,268 --> 00:24:59,336
You.

346
00:25:00,737 --> 00:25:01,571
Why would I do that?

347
00:25:02,372 --> 00:25:06,042
You said that a red sky was unrealistic
and told me to redraw a blue sky.

348
00:25:07,043 --> 00:25:09,179
-I said that?
-Yes, you, Dad.

349
00:25:12,882 --> 00:25:14,484
You don't remember it at all?

350
00:25:16,319 --> 00:25:19,923
I mean, a red sky would've been just fine.

351
00:25:20,657 --> 00:25:21,992
Right?

352
00:25:22,058 --> 00:25:23,426
That always bothered me.

353
00:25:23,493 --> 00:25:25,362
I always wondered
why the sky had to be blue.

354
00:25:26,162 --> 00:25:26,997
Yeah, why is that?

355
00:25:27,764 --> 00:25:29,065
That's what I want to know!

356
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:33,837
You should have just done
whatever you wanted.

357
00:25:33,903 --> 00:25:36,172
That wasn't the vibe at all back then.

358
00:25:36,673 --> 00:25:37,574
Not at all.

359
00:25:43,546 --> 00:25:45,248
I see…

360
00:25:51,621 --> 00:25:53,323
I guess your mom and I

361
00:25:54,457 --> 00:25:57,460
were just desperate to keep you
from straying off the path

362
00:25:58,161 --> 00:26:02,599
and to prevent you from failing.

363
00:26:06,903 --> 00:26:09,806
Are you still holding a grudge
against me for that?

364
00:26:12,842 --> 00:26:13,677
No.

365
00:26:17,781 --> 00:26:21,251
You guys put me through university,
and I was able to find a job.

366
00:26:22,352 --> 00:26:23,653
A lot happened since then,

367
00:26:25,088 --> 00:26:26,356
but it led me to where I am now.

368
00:26:28,291 --> 00:26:29,292
I'm glad.

369
00:26:31,361 --> 00:26:32,362
But

370
00:26:34,831 --> 00:26:37,734
I did to Sora the exact same thing
you did to me.

371
00:26:39,335 --> 00:26:40,470
‎What?

372
00:26:44,307 --> 00:26:46,142
To ensure he wouldn't stray from the path

373
00:26:48,445 --> 00:26:49,813
<i>and to prevent him from failing,</i>

374
00:26:52,782 --> 00:26:54,384
<i>I forced my own values upon him…</i>

375
00:26:58,655 --> 00:26:59,956
and drove Sora into a corner.

376
00:27:03,660 --> 00:27:04,594
That's

377
00:27:05,829 --> 00:27:07,230
not good.

378
00:27:14,838 --> 00:27:16,606
Although I don't want to
hear that from you.

379
00:27:21,044 --> 00:27:22,679
Was I really

380
00:27:23,913 --> 00:27:26,416
-that kind of a parent?
-Huh?

381
00:27:28,585 --> 00:27:32,922
Was I really the type
to micromanage your life?

382
00:27:32,989 --> 00:27:35,325
Yes, I never had a say in anything.

383
00:27:39,562 --> 00:27:41,064
Is that right?

384
00:27:41,131 --> 00:27:42,699
Yeah.

385
00:27:44,267 --> 00:27:46,603
I have no recollection of that at all.

386
00:27:46,669 --> 00:27:48,471
You better not forget it anymore.

387
00:27:52,642 --> 00:27:57,013
NATIONAL MATHEMATICS COMPETITION

388
00:27:58,548 --> 00:27:59,783
I'll go in now.

389
00:28:00,884 --> 00:28:03,119
Don't rush, and stay calm.

390
00:28:08,358 --> 00:28:10,627
Go get the gold medal.

391
00:28:24,174 --> 00:28:25,241
I'll do my best.

392
00:28:33,883 --> 00:28:37,487
I wonder how Umine is doing
at her mathematics competition.

393
00:28:38,154 --> 00:28:39,689
Yeah, I wonder.

394
00:28:40,857 --> 00:28:43,660
I want her to do her best, but…

395
00:28:44,227 --> 00:28:45,829
Yeah.

396
00:28:45,895 --> 00:28:47,730
I wonder if she'll be back
starting tomorrow.

397
00:28:48,832 --> 00:28:50,266
I hope so.

398
00:28:50,333 --> 00:28:54,137
I hope she doesn't end up
clinging on to Tatsuki again.

399
00:28:54,204 --> 00:28:56,873
Apparently,
one way to prevent that from happening

400
00:28:56,940 --> 00:29:00,376
is to distribute the interactions
she has with people.

401
00:29:01,077 --> 00:29:02,312
Distribute?

402
00:29:02,812 --> 00:29:05,748
It's important to reduce the time
she spends alone with Mr. Tatsuki,

403
00:29:05,815 --> 00:29:08,785
and all of us need to start
interacting with her as well.

404
00:29:10,987 --> 00:29:14,724
The idea is to "spread out
and diversify the support system."

405
00:29:14,791 --> 00:29:18,461
So, basically, all of us should
rally around Umine.

406
00:29:18,528 --> 00:29:19,596
That's right.

407
00:29:19,662 --> 00:29:22,966
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

408
00:29:23,032 --> 00:29:25,235
What are we doing for
the graduation party performance?

409
00:29:26,302 --> 00:29:29,005
We haven't talked to you guys about it.
What do you want to do?

410
00:29:29,072 --> 00:29:30,506
I want to put on a puppet show.

411
00:29:30,573 --> 00:29:32,709
-That's a good idea.
-Yeah.

412
00:29:33,376 --> 00:29:35,011
Can we join you guys too?

413
00:29:35,078 --> 00:29:36,479
-Yeah.
-Of course.

414
00:29:37,247 --> 00:29:38,715
Shi-chan and Ajicchan,

415
00:29:38,781 --> 00:29:41,384
-you guys can borrow my stuffed toys.
-Thank you.

416
00:29:41,451 --> 00:29:43,353
Do I get to play a role too?

417
00:29:44,554 --> 00:29:45,455
Let's see…

418
00:29:45,521 --> 00:29:48,191
-You can be Muscle Man.
-Muscle Man!

419
00:29:49,759 --> 00:29:51,728
I won't be using a doll then?

420
00:29:52,262 --> 00:29:53,096
Just your arms.

421
00:30:01,771 --> 00:30:03,439
Were you able to talk with your dad?

422
00:30:04,007 --> 00:30:04,874
Yes.

423
00:30:05,375 --> 00:30:06,676
<i>How did it go?</i>

424
00:30:07,410 --> 00:30:08,344
It turns out

425
00:30:09,579 --> 00:30:12,248
he doesn't remember any of that stuff
he did in the past at all.

426
00:30:12,315 --> 00:30:14,183
He was so unbothered by it,
it was anticlimactic.

427
00:30:16,419 --> 00:30:17,353
That's awesome.

428
00:30:18,254 --> 00:30:19,722
It's not funny.

429
00:30:21,324 --> 00:30:24,060
I guess it just goes to show that
even parents aren't perfect.

430
00:30:25,061 --> 00:30:26,195
Yeah.

431
00:30:28,631 --> 00:30:31,301
I gave a lot of thought regarding

432
00:30:32,435 --> 00:30:33,903
Umine and Sora.

433
00:30:35,338 --> 00:30:36,239
<i>Is that right?</i>

434
00:30:37,540 --> 00:30:40,243
There's something I want to tell Umine.

435
00:30:43,746 --> 00:30:45,315
Is it okay if I return to Yukanai?

436
00:30:47,550 --> 00:30:48,818
Okay.

437
00:30:50,053 --> 00:30:50,887
I'll pick you up.

438
00:30:52,689 --> 00:30:53,990
Thank you.

439
00:31:04,033 --> 00:31:05,301
-Okay.
-That's good.

440
00:31:05,368 --> 00:31:07,003
-Where to next?
-Right.

441
00:31:07,070 --> 00:31:08,905
-Right?
-No, left.

442
00:31:13,009 --> 00:31:14,277
Hello.

443
00:31:16,846 --> 00:31:18,815
Long time no see, Umine.

444
00:31:19,315 --> 00:31:20,750
It's been a while, Shi-chan.

445
00:31:21,250 --> 00:31:22,885
It's been a while.

446
00:31:22,952 --> 00:31:24,387
What do you want to do?

447
00:31:24,887 --> 00:31:26,990
Want to make <i>takoyaki</i>? Or popcorn?

448
00:31:27,056 --> 00:31:29,692
Let's do whatever you feel like.

449
00:31:44,707 --> 00:31:47,176
-Hey everyone, we're back.
-We're back.

450
00:31:47,243 --> 00:31:48,611
It's Tatsuki!

451
00:31:48,678 --> 00:31:50,246
-Tatsuki, you're back!
-Welcome back.

452
00:31:50,313 --> 00:31:52,081
-You're okay now?
-Yup.

453
00:31:52,148 --> 00:31:53,116
Did you bring gifts?

454
00:31:53,983 --> 00:31:55,118
Sorry, I don't have any.

455
00:31:55,685 --> 00:31:56,886
That's too bad.

456
00:31:59,088 --> 00:32:00,323
Welcome back.

457
00:32:00,823 --> 00:32:01,958
Thanks for all your help.

458
00:32:02,025 --> 00:32:03,092
It was no problem.

459
00:32:03,926 --> 00:32:05,261
Umine is here.

460
00:32:06,696 --> 00:32:08,231
Look at this.

461
00:32:08,297 --> 00:32:10,099
AWARD CERTIFICATE
MISS UMINE ANDO

462
00:32:10,166 --> 00:32:11,167
I got third place.

463
00:32:12,235 --> 00:32:13,936
You won third place? Congratulations!

464
00:32:15,004 --> 00:32:16,806
I ran out of time
and messed up at the end.

465
00:32:17,573 --> 00:32:19,042
She tried,

466
00:32:19,108 --> 00:32:20,543
but she fell just short of the goal.

467
00:32:21,577 --> 00:32:23,613
Winning a bronze medal is an amazing feat.

468
00:32:24,814 --> 00:32:26,349
Oh, I guess so.

469
00:32:28,217 --> 00:32:30,086
Hey everyone, attention please!

470
00:32:30,753 --> 00:32:31,654
What is it?

471
00:32:31,721 --> 00:32:34,123
We're going to do button art now!

472
00:32:34,190 --> 00:32:36,392
Wow, look at all those buttons.

473
00:32:36,459 --> 00:32:39,629
There are plenty of buttons,
so feel free to use as many as you like.

474
00:32:41,531 --> 00:32:43,933
Umine, want to try button art again?

475
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,369
-Yeah.
-Okay.

476
00:32:47,170 --> 00:32:49,872
All right, go ahead
and use the buttons however you like

477
00:32:49,939 --> 00:32:51,074
to express whatever you want!

478
00:32:51,140 --> 00:32:53,176
Okay!

479
00:32:58,681 --> 00:32:59,515
This is crazy.

480
00:33:01,184 --> 00:33:02,585
What should I make?

481
00:33:08,791 --> 00:33:11,994
What do you like, Umine?

482
00:33:16,732 --> 00:33:17,567
Math?

483
00:33:21,504 --> 00:33:22,572
Right now

484
00:33:24,941 --> 00:33:26,442
I don't like it that much.

485
00:33:34,817 --> 00:33:38,221
What did you like about math?

486
00:33:49,198 --> 00:33:50,199
When I was little,

487
00:33:51,634 --> 00:33:55,771
around your age, I loved to draw.

488
00:33:57,173 --> 00:33:58,307
That was because

489
00:33:59,142 --> 00:34:02,979
it allowed me to express myself freely.

490
00:34:11,787 --> 00:34:13,723
I wonder why I fell in love with math?

491
00:35:22,291 --> 00:35:25,127
Now that you’ve finished making it,
how do you feel?

492
00:35:29,665 --> 00:35:31,000
When doing math

493
00:35:34,036 --> 00:35:36,572
I liked getting
the flashes of inspiration.

494
00:35:41,444 --> 00:35:43,579
That's what made me fall in love with it.

495
00:35:46,349 --> 00:35:47,416
I see.

496
00:35:53,422 --> 00:35:54,957
But I wonder why…

497
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:06,702
I wonder why I stopped loving it.

498
00:36:22,018 --> 00:36:23,386
All right everyone,

499
00:36:23,452 --> 00:36:25,788
you can display your artwork
wherever you like.

500
00:36:26,355 --> 00:36:27,623
Okay.

501
00:36:28,124 --> 00:36:30,359
Let's display ours together.

502
00:36:30,426 --> 00:36:32,862
-You can display it wherever you want.
-Umine!

503
00:36:33,929 --> 00:36:35,698
Do you want to join our puppet show

504
00:36:35,765 --> 00:36:37,233
at the graduation party?

505
00:36:38,768 --> 00:36:41,971
You haven't been able to play at all
because of the math competition, right?

506
00:36:47,710 --> 00:36:48,911
Here.

507
00:36:51,314 --> 00:36:53,015
She wants to give it back to you.

508
00:36:56,252 --> 00:36:59,588
You're a big girl now,
so you don't need this, right?

509
00:37:03,993 --> 00:37:04,860
I…

510
00:37:06,462 --> 00:37:07,730
sold this already.

511
00:37:08,731 --> 00:37:10,333
But it's yours, Umine.

512
00:37:26,215 --> 00:37:27,049
MIDDLE SCHOOL GRADUATION PARTY

513
00:37:27,116 --> 00:37:31,354
<i>See you again, see you again</i>

514
00:37:31,420 --> 00:37:34,890
<i>No need to feel lonely anymore</i>

515
00:37:35,825 --> 00:37:39,929
<i>I'll always be here waiting for you</i>

516
00:37:39,995 --> 00:37:44,367
<i>It's okay, you can do it</i>

517
00:37:48,637 --> 00:37:49,472
All right,

518
00:37:49,538 --> 00:37:51,874
let's begin
the middle school graduation party.

519
00:37:54,944 --> 00:37:56,445
To kick things off,

520
00:37:56,512 --> 00:37:59,215
let's hear from the two students
graduating from middle school this year.

521
00:37:59,782 --> 00:38:01,784
Let's hear it for Takumi.

522
00:38:01,851 --> 00:38:03,252
Hey.

523
00:38:03,319 --> 00:38:04,987
I'm Tonetaku,
Yukanai's charismatic figure!

524
00:38:06,155 --> 00:38:06,989
That's hilarious.

525
00:38:07,056 --> 00:38:08,391
Who said you're charismatic?

526
00:38:08,457 --> 00:38:09,892
Please keep it short.

527
00:38:11,494 --> 00:38:14,797
I didn't attend middle school at all,

528
00:38:15,564 --> 00:38:17,900
so Yukanai is what I consider
my middle school.

529
00:38:19,101 --> 00:38:22,405
The precious time I spent here
with everyone

530
00:38:23,939 --> 00:38:26,008
was very…

531
00:38:27,209 --> 00:38:28,644
How should I say it…?

532
00:38:29,645 --> 00:38:31,447
-You're crying?
-Is he okay?

533
00:38:32,014 --> 00:38:34,116
-He's really crying?
-Really?

534
00:38:34,183 --> 00:38:35,351
Psyche!

535
00:38:36,919 --> 00:38:38,154
You totally got me.

536
00:38:39,588 --> 00:38:41,257
Sorry, guys.

537
00:38:41,323 --> 00:38:43,159
Let's continue being friends from now on.

538
00:38:43,225 --> 00:38:44,727
I love all of you.

539
00:38:44,794 --> 00:38:46,162
-Give me a high-five.
-Okay.

540
00:38:46,228 --> 00:38:47,129
Yeah!

541
00:38:47,196 --> 00:38:48,531
Thank you.

542
00:38:48,597 --> 00:38:50,833
Next up is Tomoki.

543
00:38:57,773 --> 00:38:58,674
If…

544
00:39:00,409 --> 00:39:02,912
I hadn't met Tatsuki and Shi-chan,

545
00:39:03,813 --> 00:39:06,248
I might not even be alive right now.

546
00:39:08,651 --> 00:39:10,152
So I'm very grateful.

547
00:39:12,321 --> 00:39:13,289
Thank you.

548
00:39:15,891 --> 00:39:17,293
You're going to make me cry.

549
00:39:17,359 --> 00:39:19,962
-Thank you, Tomoki!
-You're so cool, Tomoki.

550
00:39:20,029 --> 00:39:21,464
Someday,

551
00:39:21,964 --> 00:39:24,433
I’m going to become
the world’s number one esports player,

552
00:39:25,034 --> 00:39:26,936
become filthy rich,

553
00:39:27,503 --> 00:39:29,038
and blow everyone’s minds!

554
00:39:33,075 --> 00:39:33,943
That's awesome.

555
00:39:34,009 --> 00:39:36,946
Well, even after they graduate
middle school,

556
00:39:37,012 --> 00:39:39,381
they can drop by Yukanai
whenever they want,

557
00:39:39,448 --> 00:39:40,883
so let's all hang out again!

558
00:39:44,987 --> 00:39:46,889
And now, onto the puppet show

559
00:39:46,956 --> 00:39:49,925
"The Adventures
of the Witches Riri and Ruru."

560
00:39:50,493 --> 00:39:51,861
Ready?

561
00:39:51,927 --> 00:39:53,963
Let's begin!

562
00:39:59,168 --> 00:40:01,270
If you want to go any further,

563
00:40:01,337 --> 00:40:04,507
you must solve the question
I'm going to give you.

564
00:40:05,774 --> 00:40:08,377
Oh no! Everyone, help us figure it out.

565
00:40:09,445 --> 00:40:11,614
Okay, let's begin.

566
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:13,716
A notebook and an eraser

567
00:40:13,782 --> 00:40:16,018
cost 110 yen altogether.

568
00:40:16,085 --> 00:40:19,555
The notebook is 100 yen more expensive
than the eraser.

569
00:40:19,622 --> 00:40:20,756
Then

570
00:40:20,823 --> 00:40:23,926
how much does the eraser cost?

571
00:40:23,993 --> 00:40:25,661
-Isn't it ten yen?
-Yeah, ten yen.

572
00:40:25,728 --> 00:40:27,830
-Oh yeah?
-It's really ten yen?

573
00:40:27,897 --> 00:40:30,666
-Yeah, it's ten yen.
-Ten yen.

574
00:40:30,733 --> 00:40:33,369
It's gotta be ten yen, right?

575
00:40:33,435 --> 00:40:34,537
I got it!

576
00:40:34,603 --> 00:40:36,805
-Your answer please!
-Five yen.

577
00:40:37,506 --> 00:40:40,142
-Correct!
-Hooray!

578
00:40:53,422 --> 00:40:55,591
It’s been a long time since I’ve seen her

579
00:40:56,926 --> 00:40:58,394
look so happy.

580
00:41:00,996 --> 00:41:01,830
Yeah.

581
00:41:04,466 --> 00:41:06,602
The bridge opened up.

582
00:41:06,669 --> 00:41:07,770
In the beginning,

583
00:41:09,505 --> 00:41:11,674
whenever she was able to solve
a math problem,

584
00:41:11,740 --> 00:41:14,143
she had the look of pure joy.

585
00:41:15,844 --> 00:41:17,813
-I solved it.
-Correct.

586
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:19,848
All right!

587
00:41:23,485 --> 00:41:25,421
<i>That made me really happy too.</i>

588
00:41:27,156 --> 00:41:28,324
And I wanted

589
00:41:29,458 --> 00:41:31,093
to give her even more reasons to smile.

590
00:41:33,028 --> 00:41:34,997
What kind of a country are we in?

591
00:41:35,564 --> 00:41:37,800
It is a country that cherishes

592
00:41:37,866 --> 00:41:40,102
the things that you love.

593
00:41:41,503 --> 00:41:43,172
The things that I love…

594
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:47,343
But somewhere along the way,

595
00:41:49,511 --> 00:41:52,381
mathematics turned into
something painful for Umine.

596
00:42:00,923 --> 00:42:02,424
I took away

597
00:42:04,526 --> 00:42:05,628
something precious

598
00:42:07,796 --> 00:42:09,698
that Umine loved.

599
00:42:21,176 --> 00:42:22,111
Mr. Ando.

600
00:42:27,016 --> 00:42:28,550
You and Umine

601
00:42:31,020 --> 00:42:32,421
will be just fine.

602
00:42:38,293 --> 00:42:40,863
Ruru, what do you want to do
in this country?

603
00:42:41,497 --> 00:42:42,831
I'll think a lot.

604
00:42:44,066 --> 00:42:46,268
-I'll play a lot.
-That's nice.

605
00:42:47,670 --> 00:42:48,504
And

606
00:42:49,171 --> 00:42:50,673
I'll wait for flashes of inspiration.

607
00:42:51,907 --> 00:42:53,509
That's awesome.

608
00:42:53,575 --> 00:42:55,277
How lovely.

609
00:42:55,778 --> 00:42:56,945
That's the end of

610
00:42:57,012 --> 00:43:01,150
"The Adventures
of the Witches Riri and Ruru."

611
00:43:02,184 --> 00:43:03,652
Ready?

612
00:43:03,719 --> 00:43:06,855
Thank you very much.

613
00:43:08,557 --> 00:43:10,059
Thank you.

614
00:43:26,075 --> 00:43:27,042
Thank you.

615
00:43:27,109 --> 00:43:28,210
Not at all.

616
00:43:31,346 --> 00:43:33,048
I want to do some math quizzes
when I get home!

617
00:43:37,019 --> 00:43:37,853
Okay, let's do it.

618
00:43:42,591 --> 00:43:44,193
Bye, Tatsuki.

619
00:43:46,495 --> 00:43:48,630
Until next time, Umine.

620
00:43:52,434 --> 00:43:53,669
Let's go, Daddy.

621
00:43:59,608 --> 00:44:01,744
All right, shall we clean up?

622
00:44:02,244 --> 00:44:03,312
Yeah.

623
00:44:18,460 --> 00:44:19,461
YU
13 MISSED CALLS

624
00:44:21,630 --> 00:44:22,631
YU

625
00:44:34,042 --> 00:44:34,910
Please, stop.

626
00:44:37,346 --> 00:44:38,614
Stop this, Sora.

627
00:44:47,422 --> 00:44:48,857
-What the hell, damn it!
-Sora!

628
00:44:53,662 --> 00:44:54,596
Hey.

629
00:44:56,231 --> 00:44:57,232
What are you doing?

630
00:45:01,970 --> 00:45:03,272
Shut up!

631
00:45:08,076 --> 00:45:09,945
I wonder where we went wrong.

632
00:45:10,012 --> 00:45:11,146
THIS DRAMA IS FICTIONAL

633
00:45:11,213 --> 00:45:14,550
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita

